lections"}, {"submitted_answer_id": "8dfee409-bf56-5694-acbf-98c6ca8e711f", "expected": "rejected", "purpose": "all radio selections"}]}, {"label": "signed/q-48631", "record": {"knowledge_point": {"db_id": 17592186092261, "id": "2f4bfd24-dafd-57b3-940a-154a6e0acf3d", "title": "Differentiating a General Exponential Function Using the Chain Rule"}, "question": {":question/id": "b8b8d559-9327-580a-83b2-460dc4fb2ae7", ":question/problem": "Given that $y = 6^{-9x^{2} - 4}$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$.", ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny={6}^{u},\\,u=-9x^{2} - 4.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}={6}^{u}\\ln(6),\\,\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=-18x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x} & =\\frac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x} \\\\ & ={6}^{u}\\ln(6)\\cdot (-18x) \\\\ & =(-18x)\\cdot {6}^{u}\\ln(6) \\\\ & =-18x\\cdot {6}^{-9x^{2} - 4}\\ln(6).\\end{aligned}\n$$", ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy", ":question/answer-fields": [{":answer-field/id": "dc5e09e9-3785-558c-af68-2906ea29eed8", ":answer-field/key": "selection", ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio", ":answer-field/choices": [{":answer/id": "ce68f6af-d7b2-5632-9047-524567bb9392", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "6^{- 9 x^{2} - 4} \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}"}, {":answer/id": "c6e94d11-fb10-5c23-8069-6c2d2741f72a", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "- 18 \\cdot 6^{- 9 x^{2} - 4} x"}, {":answer/id": "78de4681-0efb-56d9-953b-0608f48f7b75", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "- 18 \\cdot 6^{- 9 x^{2} - 4} x \\ln{\\left(6 \\right)}"}, {":answer/id": "d70c6e79-7b1b-5bbd-810b-41fa4f1ef6f8", ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math", ":answer/value": "- 18 \\cdot 6^{- 9 x^{2} - 5} x \\left(- 9 x^{2} - 4\\right)"}, {":answer/id": "9982799a-db90-5045-a05b-c2521e